<title>USA: Dionex Corp Q2 Dec 31 net income rises.</title>
<headline>Dionex Corp Q2 Dec 31 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 Mos ended 12/31    6 Mos ended 12/31</p>
<p>				   1996	1995    1996	  1995</p>
<p> Net sales		   $36,600  $34,010 $68,108     $64,066</p>
<p> Gross profit		 25,516   23,495  47,370	43,883</p>
<p> Total operating expenses 15,401   14,841  29,639	28,947</p>
<p> Operating income	   10,115    8,654  17,731	14,936</p>
<p> Interest income, net	  340	532     664	 1,067</p>
<p>Income before taxes</p>
<p>  on income		   10,455    9,186  18,395	16,003</p>
<p> Taxes on income	     3,607    3,192   6,346	 5,561</p>
<p> Net income		    6,848    5,994  12,049	10,442</p>
<p> Net EPS			   .54	.43     .94	   .75</p>
<p>Common shrs used in computing</p>
<p>  per share amounts	 12,698   13,910  12,809	13,999</p>
<p>		  (In thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Company said If currency rates had remained unchanged, sales growth would have been higher, at 11 percent.</p>
<p>Company repurchased 317,300 shares of its common stock during the second quarter of fiscal 1997 under its share repurchase programs, bringing the cumulative repurchases in fiscal 1997 to 556,800 shares.</p>
</text>
